Title:
capa-cpp — Targeted C++ reimplementation of Mandiant CAPA (CLI + IDA Pro plugin)

Type:
GitHub Tool

Short Summary (4-8 sentences max):
capa-cpp is a C++ reimplementation of Mandiant’s capa capability-matching engine that loads native capa rules and aims for match parity in specific workflows. It focuses on extracting features (API calls, strings, numbers, disassembly-derived artifacts) from multiple backends—especially Microsoft Time Travel Debugging (TTD) artifacts, Windows process minidumps, and IDA databases—then matching capa rules across file/function/basic-block/instruction scopes. The project provides a standalone CLI for TTD reports/manifests and minidumps, plus an IDA Pro plugin that displays and can annotate matches in the database. It’s designed to be driven by other tooling (e.g., ttd-capa) rather than as a general-purpose capa replacement for all formats. Notably, it supports scanning reconstructed code from TTD snapshots (unpacked/injected/JIT’d) via Zydis disassembly and can analyze private RWX regions in full dumps. Useful for reverse engineers, malware analysts, and red/blue teams who want fast, automatable capability triage inside IDA or from dynamic trace artifacts.

Technical Focus:
- CAPA rule loading and capability matching engine (subscopes, rule parity goals)
- Feature extraction from TTD (API-call reports and reconstructed code manifests/snapshots)
- Minidump parsing (modules/regions) and disassembly with Zydis
- IDA Pro integration (CFG/imports/exports/strings/FLIRT) and match annotation
- Output control for scale (JSON/MessagePack, matches-only, evidence tree limiting)

Use Cases:
- Triage malware behavior/capabilities from TTD-recorded API call traces
- Scan reconstructed runtime code (unpacked/injected/JIT) from TTD snapshots for capabilities
- Identify capabilities in memory-resident payloads/shellcode via full process minidumps (including RWX regions)
- Run capa-style capability tagging directly inside IDA and annotate findings for RE workflows
- Automate large-scale analysis pipelines with compact outputs (MessagePack, matches-only)

Keywords:
capa, Mandiant, capa-rules, capability detection, rule engine, feature extraction, Time Travel Debugging, TTD, ttd-capa, minidump, process memory dump, RWX, shellcode, IDA Pro plugin, ida-sdk, Zydis, disassembly, FLIRT, JSON, MessagePack